agent: GitHub Actions Coding Standard applies to **Create the weekly restock workflow**. The workflow will use the required `.github/workflows/<name>.yml` location, full commit-SHA action pins, repository secrets, and a job timeout.
  YAML Coding Standard applies to **Create the weekly restock workflow**. The workflow will use two-space indentation and contain no encrypted values.
  GitHub’s documentation confirms scheduled workflows use POSIX cron syntax and that scheduled runs default to UTC unless a timezone is specified. It also recommends pinning actions to full commit SHAs. [Workflow syntax](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-syntax), [secure use](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use)
  The order service and store mail service are internal services whose vendor documentation could not be confirmed.
  **Here is a proposed starting point for your codify feature:**
  **Title:** Run the weekly restock alert
  **Summary:** Send the scheduled email listing items at or below their reorder point.
  **Description:** Each Monday at 06:00, GitHub Actions will query the order service with a read-only token, format items needing restock, and send one email to the warehouse lead.
  **Acceptance criteria:**
  - One scheduled Monday run sends one email containing every item at or below its reorder point.
  **Executor:** GitHub Actions
  **Diagram:**
  ```flowchart TB
    P["GitHub Actions"] -->|Create the weekly restock workflow| T1["Restock alert workflow"]
  ```
  **Tasks:**
  1. **Create the weekly restock workflow:**
     - **Scope:** Schedule the Monday check, query stock levels without writing them, format items at or below their reorder point, and send one email to the warehouse lead.
     - **Provider:** GitHub Actions
     - **Method:** GitHub Actions scheduled workflow using the order service `GET /stock?below=reorder` endpoint and the store’s mail service; credentials come from repository secrets.
     - **Standards:**
       1. GitHub Actions Coding Standard
       2. YAML Coding Standard
     - **Files:**
       1. `.github/workflows/restock-alert.yml`
     - **Assumptions:**
       - The order service endpoint and store mail service are available.
       - The warehouse lead’s email address and read-only stock token are configured as repository secrets.
       - The schedule’s 06:00 timezone is explicitly configured for the intended business timezone.
  **Controls and NFRs:**
  - Protect Customer Payment Data
  - Order Service Monthly Availability
  **Proposed project:** New `restock-alerts`
  **Rationale:** This folder is the right home because it contains the weekly restock alert automation and its workflow.
  **What would you add, correct, or remove?**
  If this is accurate, just say so. Highway will use this specification to build out the solution.
